course: dictionary
lesson: 5093
title: One word, three meanings: intent
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Intent is one of these. Look at the words around it first. «The man was caught with intent to steal.» Here intent means the plan or purpose in someone's mind.
explain: «She was intent on winning the race.» Intent on means very determined to do something. The word on is a clue. Try your meaning in the sentence: she was very determined to win, and that makes sense.
explain: «His eyes were intent on the screen.» Intent can also describe close attention. Intent eyes are focused on one thing, with the mind fully on it. The clue is the screen: he is watching it closely.
explain: Some phrases use intent in special ways. «To all intents and purposes» means in almost every way. «An honest mistake» is a mistake made without bad intent, so nobody meant any harm. When you are unsure, read the whole sentence and swap in your meaning.
fact: Intent is a noun meaning what someone means or plans to do, or their purpose.
fact: «With intent to steal» means the person planned to steal, on purpose.
fact: «Intent on» is a phrase meaning very determined to do something.
fact: «An intent look» means a look that pays very close attention.
fact: «To all intents and purposes» means in almost every way; «with good intent» means meaning well.
exercise: «The crime was committed with intent to harm.» What does intent mean here? | A loud noise | A small piece of paper | A feeling of tiredness | *A plan or purpose to do something
exercise: «She was intent on winning the race.» What does intent on mean? | Lost on the way home | *Very determined to do something | Bored and sleepy
exercise: «His eyes were intent on the screen.» What does intent suggest? | Feeling sick after lunch | Closing his eyes to sleep | Looking away from the screen | *Paying very close attention
test: «An honest mistake» is one made without bad intent. What does bad intent mean? | Being too quick to finish | *Planning to do harm on purpose | Making a mess by accident | Not knowing the answer
test: Mum says, «Your plan has good intent, love.» What does good intent mean? | Being very tired | *Meaning well, with a kind purpose | Being very loud | Winning a prize
exam: Which phrase means in almost every way? | With intent | An intent look | *To all intents and purposes | Intent on
